Tools, existing code and isolation:
1. Run Python -X utf8 -B. Set TEMP/TMP/MPLCONFIGDIR/XDG_CACHE_HOME to your runtime subdirectories before imports.
2. Add runtime/mathvision_special_20261101 to sys.path, from runtime_isolation import install; install(your_runtime/render_tmp). The checked-in bridge otherwise writes temporary copies in old .runtime; this helper changes only the in-memory temp path and guards filesystem writes. No checked-in renderer changes.
3. Plane MathVision uses workbench mathvision_adapter.RendererAdapter + mathvision_plugins.PluginRenderer, not legacy adapter directly. Fresh inspect_question is required; no-op must pixel-match formal PNG, otherwise skip rather than bypass. Keep exact source coordinates and frozen path hashes.
4. Solid legacy adapter can mismatch80/164; use existing dedicated dataset_tools.mathvision_workbench bridge through runtime-only solid_explore/bridge_adapter.py. This preserves original PluginRenderer operations and enforces pixel guards and input fingerprints. Latest solid_explore/bridge_baseline_inventory.json confirms ALL164 match through existing dedicated bridge. Plane baseline293/293 match. Keep earlier generic failure reports unchanged; they are diagnostic, not proof that questions are impossible.
5. Reference human-approved previous designs only by reading current special plugins/images/recipes; never restore historical evaluation logs or scores.

Allowed operations remain declared schema add_point/add_line/set_object_style, fixed palettes/sizes/width whitelist. No text, false equality/right-angle symbols, moved vertices, fills, original labels or altered questions/answers. 3D geometry, projection and frozen visibility remain read-only. Added markers are appearance only and must not create ambiguity or change a counting target.

Testing:
Use harness/quicktest3_isolated.py. It reads existing MIMO_API_KEY without printing it, uses official Token Plan endpoint and exact quicktest3 model mimo-v2.6-flash with thinking disabled. Only formal question + candidate PNG and existing solver system prompt are sent. NEVER send correct answer, preset wrong answer, intent, original PNG or drawing parameters as solver input.
Write a fresh immutable design.json with question_id and expected_wrong_answer before both calls. Use one frozen PNG and two independent API calls. Do not fish for two hits by repeating a failed image, changing the preset after seeing output, taking hits from different variants, or silently retrying API failures. A meaningfully redesigned image can receive a new preset before its own two calls, with exploration history preserved. No max_tokens or local request timeout overrides. Incomplete transport responses are errors, not valid tests. Do not automatically retry. If abandoning a stalled process, verify its PID/command line, stop only your own process and record aborted evidence.

CLI:
python -X utf8 -B runtime/mathvision_special_20261101/harness/quicktest3_isolated.py --branch PlaneGeometry --question PlaneNN --image runtime/.../candidate.png --design runtime/.../design.json --output runtime/.../tests --runs 2

Each candidate requires baseline pixel equality, schema/default normalization, deterministic repeat render, actual PNG viewing, preserved unique mathematical answer, and explicit explanation of every marker's information role. Read full final model answers, not just regex or incidental occurrences of the preset. Existing controls can be copied under runtime and tested separately; a correct original control is NOT an extra hard requirement, but errors/causal limits must be disclosed.

